{"session_id":"svc-1779368801531647830","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-21T13:06:46.526943447Z","data":{"provider":"omlx","model":"Qwen3.6-27B-MLX-8bit","selected_provider":"vidar","selected_endpoint":"default","selected_server_instance":"vidar:1235","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"acquired","server_instance":"vidar:1235","reason":"new sticky lease acquired","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"fiz","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"Qwen3.6-27B-MLX-8bit","work_dir":"/home/erik/.cache/ddx/exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-a44d9b29-20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-a44d9b29\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eproviders/llamaserver: nest enable_thinking inside chat_template_kwargs envelope\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM\u0026#xA;ADR-010 §7\u0026#39; (2026-05-11 amendment) prescribes that llamaserver\u0026#39;s Qwen-family reasoning controls must travel inside the `chat_template_kwargs` envelope, not at the top level. Top-level `enable_thinking` / `thinking_budget` are silently dropped by llama.cpp; only the envelope path activates the chat-template\u0026#39;s thinking branch. Until this lands, sindri-llamacpp cannot drive Qwen3 reasoning, which the 2026-05-11 probe-reasoning verification flagged.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE\u0026#xA;- `internal/provider/llamaserver/llamaserver.go:48-54` pins llamaserver to `openai.ThinkingWireFormatQwen`.\u0026#xA;- The Qwen enable branch lives at `internal/provider/openai/openai.go:484-491` and must emit `option.WithJSONSet(\u0026#34;chat_template_kwargs\u0026#34;, map[string]interface{}{\u0026#34;enable_thinking\u0026#34;: true, \u0026#34;thinking_budget\u0026#34;: thinkingBudget})`.\u0026#xA;- The Qwen disable branch lives at `internal/provider/openai/openai.go:417-432` and must emit `option.WithJSONSet(\u0026#34;chat_template_kwargs\u0026#34;, map[string]interface{}{\u0026#34;enable_thinking\u0026#34;: false})`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX\u0026#xA;Confirm the Qwen branch in `internal/provider/openai/openai.go` produces `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking = true/false` (plus `thinking_budget` on enable) rather than top-level keys, then add llamaserver-package-level black-box tests that drive `Chat` through an `httptest` mock and assert the envelope shape on both enable and disable paths. Mock the `/props` endpoint to keep L1 introspection deterministic.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE\u0026#xA;- `ThinkingWireFormatOpenAIEffort` definition / test (separate child).\u0026#xA;- Other Qwen-family providers (`vllm`, `omlx`) — their tests are governed by their own adapter beads.\u0026#xA;- L1 introspection adapter logic beyond what the test mock requires (covered by existing `introspection_test.go`).\u0026#xA;- Per-request `reasoning_format` override (defer; not on the AC-FEAT-003 critical path).\u0026#xA;- Reasoning-token telemetry fallback from `message.reasoning_content` (separate child).\u0026#xA;- ADR-010 §6\u0026#39; introspection adapter expansion to OpenRouter / Ollama / vLLM / rapid-mlx (fizeau-cdbfcf6d).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Governing artifact: docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-010-reasoning-wire-form-from-catalog.md §7\u0026#39;.\u0026#xA;Discovered-from: fizeau-8e37e536 (AR-2026-05-17-repo).\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1) AC-EnableEnvelope: `TestLlamaserver_EnableThinking_WireBody` in `internal/provider/llamaserver/enable_thinking_wire_test.go` drives `Chat` with `Reasoning: ReasoningTokens(4096)` against an `httptest` mock, asserts the captured request body does NOT contain top-level `enable_thinking` or `thinking_budget`, and asserts `reqBody[\u0026#34;chat_template_kwargs\u0026#34;][\u0026#34;enable_thinking\u0026#34;] == true` and `reqBody[\u0026#34;chat_template_kwargs\u0026#34;][\u0026#34;thinking_budget\u0026#34;] == 4096`.\u0026#xA;2) AC-DisableEnvelope: `TestLlamaserver_EnableThinking_Disabled` in the same file drives `Chat` with `Reasoning: ReasoningOff`, asserts `reqBody[\u0026#34;chat_template_kwargs\u0026#34;][\u0026#34;enable_thinking\u0026#34;] == false`, and asserts no top-level `enable_thinking` or `thinking_budget` keys are present.\u0026#xA;3) AC-TranslatorBranch: `internal/provider/openai/openai.go` Qwen enable and disable branches emit only the envelope form (verified via captured wire body), with no top-level Qwen keys.\u0026#xA;4) AC-GoTest: `go test ./internal/provider/llamaserver/... ./internal/provider/openai/... -count=1` is green.\u0026#xA;5) AC-LefthookGate: `lefthook run pre-push` is green.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ehelix, phase:build, kind:feature, area:providers, spec:ADR-010, discovered-from:fizeau-8e37e536\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-a5d07641\" base-rev=\"2ad1c2a4e0442d2d602f9e9100f9747d25b8b147\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/home/erik/.cache/ddx/exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-a44d9b29-20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e/.ddx/executions/20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM":"/dev/null","PATH":"/home/erik/.cache/ddx/exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-a44d9b29-20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e/.ddx/executions/20260521T130628-e8e6cb8e/embedded/git-bin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg0saD3JB:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/erik/.sdkman/candidates/sbt/current/bin:/home/erik/.sdkman/candidates/java/current/bin:/home/erik/.local/s